WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.090
- Mama's going to love it.

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:02.440
- [Hannah] Oh, look it.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.290
Get outta there.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.123
- This is hard.

00:00:04.123 --> 00:00:05.450
- Nothing tastes better than food

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.760
somebody else cooked for you.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.050
He's never made it before.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.388
Henry!

00:00:10.388 --> 00:00:13.100
I do appreciate his creative toppings.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.080
- Tomatoes!

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.350
- [Hannah] It was beautiful.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.380
I was so pampered that day. (laughs)

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.330
How's the soup, Wy?

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.273
Hi, I'm Hannah.

00:00:20.273 --> 00:00:21.680
I'm The World's OK-est Mom

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.290
and I get a lot of comments
saying that it looks

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.100
like I'm the only person
in my house who ever cooks.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.930
Now, that's not true, but
it did get me thinking

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.230
that maybe it's time for
you to see what it looks

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.960
like when the boys in
my house do the cooking.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.870
So for an entire week,
I'm out of the kitchen.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.900
I don't even know what to expect here,

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.840
so please wish me luck.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.640
This is probably your
mother requested episode.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.060
The thing that makes me the most nervous

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.300
about this week is I'm in
charge of cleanup duty.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.560
I am a cook who cleans as I go.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.990
And Matt doesn't do that.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:56.220
He cooks through the whole
meal and then tackles the rest

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.053
at the end.

00:00:57.053 --> 00:00:59.220
I have so much fun in the
kitchen with the boys.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.080
And so my hope is that Matt

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.290
and the boys get that
amazing bonding time.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.130
And I'm excited to see
what they come up with.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.820
- Tonight, we have to cook mama dinner.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.489
It's all on us.

00:01:09.489 --> 00:01:10.579
What do you want to cook her?

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:11.981
- Steak?

00:01:11.981 --> 00:01:13.180
- Yeah steak, right?

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.013
- Fancy

00:01:14.013 --> 00:01:15.280
- That's good. She'll like steak.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.600
And what else?

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.274
We gotta do a vegetable, right?

00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:19.107
- Yeah. Broccoli!

00:01:19.107 --> 00:01:20.270
- Broccoli!

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.110
- Yeah!

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:21.943
High fives!

00:01:21.943 --> 00:01:23.930
- Day one started off
pretty easy for Matt.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.210
He leaned into his strengths
and he fired up the grill.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.260
- [Matt] Scrub it good, we gotta clean it!

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.650
- [Hannah] Sweet Matt, are you vlogging?

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.694
- [Matt] Yeah. Are you spying on me?

00:01:32.694 --> 00:01:33.527
(Hannah laughing)

00:01:33.527 --> 00:01:34.930
- [Hannah] That's my job.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:35.870
I was a little nervous

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.870
about him letting Jackson and Wyatt help

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:41.210
out around the hot grill,
but all went smoothly.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.150
- [Matt] Good job, guys!

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.060
- [Hannah] There's not much

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.560
that the boys can do to help
when it comes to grilling.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.190
Cause a lot of it is just
flipping and monitoring.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.010
So they did what they could.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.100
I really thought I was going
to have an easy this week

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.900
but I was on Henry duty

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.160
for most of the time during meal prep.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.570
No, Wyatt, Wyatt, no. Nope.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.100
Usually that's my time
to have a little break

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.740
and I can kind of Zen
out and do some cooking.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.253
This time I was on full Henry duty.

00:02:06.168 --> 00:02:07.630
There's your dad.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.680
Look at him with his flashlight grilling.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.080
Oh, look it.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.300
The dinner was delicious.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.720
I was really happy that
they thought of a vegetable,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.610
and a protein and they even
had a side of potato salad.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.519
How much did you guys help?

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:22.352
- Eight percent.

00:02:22.352 --> 00:02:23.230
- [Hannah] Okay.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.840
The one thing that wasn't the most

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.560
conscious was the budget.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.510
I mean, those stakes were a
little pricey, but I'm not

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.510
going to complain because
they were delicious.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.343
Thank you.

00:02:33.343 --> 00:02:34.310
- You're welcome.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:39.270
- Very windy day, but they're
outside cooking again.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:43.180
Poured myself a little glass
of wine and now I'm going to

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.980
drink it while someone else cooks for me.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.390
I think Matt's thinking was I
started out strong on day one.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.210
So let's just grill again on day two.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.700
Cheese veggie dogs,

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.640
and some cut up pickles

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.632
Are we having a vegetable?

00:02:58.632 --> 00:02:59.465
(record scratch)

00:02:59.465 --> 00:03:00.370
- [Matt] Ummm..

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.203
Guys.

00:03:03.153 --> 00:03:05.980
- Matt says the vegetable is the pickles.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.320
And I know they love me

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.230
because they made these

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.420
and no one else really likes them but me.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.560
Usually when I cook

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.570
I make foods that I know
everyone else will enjoy.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.290
So it was nice as the
tables turned for mealtime

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.173
Look who's trolling. Rosie!

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.890
I think he likes it.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.794
Can I have some kranch on mine?

00:03:23.794 --> 00:03:24.632
- [Matt] You want kranch?

00:03:24.632 --> 00:03:25.465
- Yeah!

00:03:25.465 --> 00:03:26.480
- [Hannah] Yeah, I want kranch.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.680
This is kranch, it's ketchup ranch.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.270
And it is divine.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.860
And I just like saying it.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.778
How could you be mad when you've
got kranch in your fridge?

00:03:35.778 --> 00:03:36.890
Oh yeah.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.980
We were in LA, we were at my mom's house.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.920
Day three. We packed everything in the car

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.560
and drove to LA because

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.380
at the end of the week it
would actually be Mother's Day.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.540
So we wanted to be there

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.890
with my mom and make it
a big family gathering.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.540
Matt and the boys decided to
make one of Matt's specialties.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.340
He loves to make tortilla soup.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.823
- [Matt] Put the beans
in there, boy. Yeah!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.560
Thank you!

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.420
- Oh it smells good!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.940
- [ Hannah] His secret that he swears

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.430
by is taking corn tortillas
and sticking them right

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.500
in the soup and letting
them dissolve to thicken it.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.300
- [Matt] Oh, it's on a little boat.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:11.660
Tortilla boat

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:12.960
- Soup was spectacular.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.440
He's really, really good at it.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.360
And it never turns out the same way twice.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.390
He just kind of goes

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.370
and put stuff in and it turns
into something delicious.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.960
This is so good.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.963
Ten out of ten, Matt.

00:04:25.577 --> 00:04:29.560
What are we thinking
about, oh Jackson finished?

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.393
- Oh yeah.

00:04:30.393 --> 00:04:32.590
- [Hannah] Wy? What do you think?

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.730
Wyatt gets really overwhelmed

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:36.930
by a big looking amount of food.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.850
He likes little bites.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:43.130
So I just got this plate, but
basically you put the food

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:46.370
in each container and then
there's a treasure in here

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:49.600
and this has been amazing
for Wyatt cause he loves it.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.433
Right?

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:55.380
Once I moved it into that
plate, he enjoyed it so much.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.570
Total mom hack.

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:58.620
It's one of the most
brilliant things I've seen

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.700
in a very long time.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:00.723
How's the soup, Wy?

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.614
I smell something what's cooking?

00:05:04.614 --> 00:05:05.510
- [Matt] You'll find out.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.343
- [Hannah] I'm gonna look.

00:05:06.343 --> 00:05:07.940
- [Matt] No, no, no! Get out of there.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.960
- I'm looking.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.079
Oh, French fries.

00:05:10.079 --> 00:05:11.320
Whoa!

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.680
They're dark.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:13.820
Are you over cooking them?

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:14.653
- No

00:05:14.653 --> 00:05:16.649
- What did you forget to do?

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.105
- Turn them.

00:05:18.105 --> 00:05:19.730
- He didn't turn them.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:20.563
This is the thing --

00:05:20.563 --> 00:05:23.375
- [Matt] You know, I actually
like things that are more

00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:24.208
brown.

00:05:24.208 --> 00:05:26.540
- He does this every time.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.330
You know, he'll make a
mistake in the kitchen

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.880
but it's I like it.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.310
So keep going.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.940
I think it's something he
passed along to the boys.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:38.331
- I totally meant to make
her waffles kind of frozen.

00:05:38.331 --> 00:05:39.750
Totally meant to do that.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:40.940
- [Hannah] What are you doing?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.130
- Just cutting up my french fry pizza.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.900
- [Hannah] French fry pizza?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.240
They decided they wanted
to make French fry pizza.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.600
It's something that I make
with them quite a bit.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.930
So of course they asked
Matt to try to make it.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.360
He's never made it before.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:54.997
What did you put on it?

00:05:54.997 --> 00:05:55.920
- [Matt] Olives.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.740
- [Hannah] This antipasto mix?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:58.573
- [Matt] Yeah.

00:05:58.573 --> 00:06:01.596
- [Hannah] Wow. And you
cooked it in a cake pan.

00:06:01.596 --> 00:06:02.429
- [Matt] Yup.

00:06:02.429 --> 00:06:03.430
- [Hannah] All right...

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.240
Not the most aesthetic French fry pizza

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.670
but it tasted amazing.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.700
It's actually sticking together kind of

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.200
which is surprising to me.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.860
Okay.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.503
Seven point five out of ten.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.362
Did you enjoy yours?

00:06:17.362 --> 00:06:18.230
(Henry babbling)

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.010
- The boys were so happy to have it.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:22.083
They'd wanted it for a really long time.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:23.900
Are you proud of it?

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.170
- Yeah. So good.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.100
- Day five. I decided
to make a food request.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:32.485
I would like a french omelet this morning.

00:06:32.485 --> 00:06:33.690
- What's a french omelet?

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:34.523
- A french omelet?

00:06:34.523 --> 00:06:35.356
- I've never had one.

00:06:35.356 --> 00:06:36.570
I've just seen pictures of it.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.510
- [Matt] Are they the
little rolled up ones?

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:39.343
- [Hannah] So you know what it is.

00:06:39.343 --> 00:06:40.373
- [Matt] Yeah.

00:06:41.539 --> 00:06:43.930
We're going to have Jackson
do the cracking, I think.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.477
And you'll do the whisking.

00:06:46.483 --> 00:06:47.620
- Get the whisk!

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.523
- [Matt] Okay, Wyatt, you
ready to start whisking?

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.920
Right, Wyatt, good job, buddy!

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.590
- While they're making the French omelets.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:58.670
I'm with Henry.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:06:59.503
- Bah!

00:06:59.503 --> 00:07:00.840
- Bar, you've got a bar.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.640
He is really silly.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.010
He's a really silly kid

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:04.950
and he's a lot of fun.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:05.783
Who's that?

00:07:06.975 --> 00:07:07.808
- Baba.

00:07:07.808 --> 00:07:08.641
- Baby!

00:07:08.641 --> 00:07:09.723
Blow a kiss to baby?

00:07:11.127 --> 00:07:12.786
So sweet.

00:07:12.786 --> 00:07:16.450
- [Matt] So the tricky part
will be to try to, to roll this.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.283
Oh my gosh.

00:07:17.283 --> 00:07:18.290
Oh, I almost had it.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.300
- [Hannah] The sounds coming

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.790
from the kitchen when they
were doing the flip was

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:25.300
like someone had just
scored the winning touchdown

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:26.637
at the super bowl.

00:07:26.637 --> 00:07:27.470
- Oh!

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:31.137
(Matt and Jackson cheering)

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.330
- [Matt] We add something to the top.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:34.163
What are these?

00:07:35.176 --> 00:07:36.532
- Uh, micro greens?

00:07:36.532 --> 00:07:37.365
- [Matt] Micro greens?

00:07:37.365 --> 00:07:38.198
- Yeah.

00:07:38.198 --> 00:07:40.497
- [Matt] We're just gonna put
the little green parts on it.

00:07:40.497 --> 00:07:42.400
Not the twigs.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.870
- Oh my gosh.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:45.970
This looks amazing!

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.370
Did I enjoy it?

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.203
A hundred percent.

00:07:48.203 --> 00:07:50.959
It was great. It was a
really, really buttery omelet.

00:07:50.959 --> 00:07:51.792
- [Matt] Is it good?

00:07:51.792 --> 00:07:52.625
Oh that is good.

00:07:52.625 --> 00:07:53.458
Thank you boys.

00:07:53.458 --> 00:07:55.270
This is my dream fulfilled.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.320
Henry is what's yours is mine

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.360
through and through the second they

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:00.910
laid those eggs in front of me.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:05.000
He goes with his whole hand
and grabs my entire omelet to

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.350
try to start leading it like a burrito.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:09.050
I'm in for it with this kid.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.864
I hear some struggling happening

00:08:10.864 --> 00:08:11.697
(Boys struggling)

00:08:11.697 --> 00:08:12.530
in the kitchen.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:13.950
So I feel like I should help.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:18.200
The day six, I was not clued
into what was being prepared

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.493
but clearly the boys all had big plans.

00:08:21.493 --> 00:08:22.326
(laughs) What are you

00:08:22.326 --> 00:08:23.159
watching?

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:25.643
- God.

00:08:25.643 --> 00:08:27.890
- Matt comes in, he's got a coconut

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:30.640
and a big knife and I'm thinking

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:33.430
what could you possibly
be making with this?

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.295
- What?

00:08:34.295 --> 00:08:35.486
(laughs)

00:08:35.486 --> 00:08:36.319
(Matt yells)

00:08:36.319 --> 00:08:37.363
- [Hannah] Why coconut?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.860
- They're struggling with the knife.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.445
So Jackson and Wyatt had
this brilliant idea to

00:08:45.445 --> 00:08:48.288
chuck it outside, to try to break it.

00:08:48.288 --> 00:08:49.121
- [Matt] Oh my gosh!

00:08:49.121 --> 00:08:50.890
- Oh my god I heard the liquid.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.100
- They finally got the coconut open

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.890
and I still had no idea
what they were using for.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:09:00.460
Is this like your fuel,
to make something else?

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:01.818
- We're going to use the meat.

00:09:01.818 --> 00:09:03.910
Let's the squeeze some
oranges and some lemons.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:06.380
- [Jackson] I'm gonna put
cilantro into the bowl.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.710
- [Hannah] They're chopping tomatoes,

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.070
they're chopping onions.

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:10.510
I don't understand how that goes

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:11.810
along with coconut.

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:12.740
- Tomatoes.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.640
- Ooh. Special delivery.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.200
They were making vegan ceviche.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.760
I'm so excited.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:19.593
Oh my gosh.

00:09:19.593 --> 00:09:21.820
I have never really had much ceviche

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:24.350
cause it always has shrimp in it!

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:25.183
Thank you.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.633
Okay. Let's try it.

00:09:30.699 --> 00:09:32.670
It's hard to believe this is coconut.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.680
Ooh, this is good, you guys.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.300
I felt really special.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.380
You know, Matt thought of the recipe.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.240
He thought of my dietary restrictions.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.110
The boys actually enjoyed it.

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:45.070
I was really surprised
because it had a lot

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:47.627
of ingredients that Wyatt
definitely won't touch

00:09:47.627 --> 00:09:49.010
but it's that thing

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:52.190
of when he helps he's way
more willing to taste it.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:54.096
Thank you I appreciate this!

00:09:54.096 --> 00:09:54.929
- You're welcome.

00:09:54.929 --> 00:09:56.240
It was delicious.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.640
It's Mother's day.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:09:59.600
I have my coffee and my mask

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.650
and the boys are making
some sort of complex brunch.

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.440
They decided to make eggs benedict

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:07.700
because to them it's an
exciting breakfast food.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:10.780
And I know Matt especially
loves eggs benedict

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:13.550
For a beginner cook eggs
benedict is pretty difficult.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:17.040
There are many points at
which the recipe can go south.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.860
And unfortunately for Matt

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.530
he pretty much went south at all of them.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:24.419
I can't not say something.
Oh my god. Matt!

00:10:24.419 --> 00:10:25.568
- [Matt] Oh I didn't swirl it.

00:10:25.568 --> 00:10:27.428
(bleep) (bleep)

00:10:27.428 --> 00:10:31.960
- Matt! Oh my God, he's
trying to poach eggs.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.650
And all he's doing is spooning.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:34.833
The yolks.

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:39.000
That's all the egg whites. Matt!

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:39.833
Can I help you?

00:10:39.833 --> 00:10:40.930
Can I show you one?

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:43.030
I didn't want him to get too discouraged

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.470
with the recipe and I
didn't want to deter him

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.300
from trying new recipes in the future.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:50.370
So I offered to teach him
how to poach one egg just

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:53.130
so he could see a clear example
and then he could take it

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:54.010
and go from there.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:55.980
And then drop the egg in. Okay.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.427
- [Jackson] Oh my god.

00:10:57.427 --> 00:11:00.830
- [Jackson And Wyatt] Three! Two! One!

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:02.780
- [Hannah] Once he saw
the first one being made,

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:03.910
he knew what to do

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:05.770
and he did a really good job for the rest.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.470
Arguably, the hardest part

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.482
of eggs Benedict is the hollandaise sauce.

00:11:10.482 --> 00:11:11.482
- [Matt] Oh,

00:11:13.386 --> 00:11:14.250
oh my goodness.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:15.177
Okay! You did it.

00:11:15.177 --> 00:11:16.140
- No shells.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.969
- [Matt] No shells! (laughs)

00:11:17.969 --> 00:11:19.580
- Dijon mustard.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.110
- [Matt] No, no, no. No, nope.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.410
Just.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.080
- Let's just say in the kitchen,

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.660
Matt's probably not the most
clear communicator and Jackson

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.120
isn't the best listener.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.170
So it really wasn't the best combo to

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.990
make something as complex
as hollandaise sauce.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.880
- [Matt] This is for the holiday sauce.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:37.819
Hollandaise.

00:11:37.819 --> 00:11:40.350
- [Hannah] Holiday sauce (laughs)

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.950
- [Matt] Can you stop
talking in the background?

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:44.260
- Matt is stressed.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.120
He was like muttering to himself

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:48.420
and making frustrated noises.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.532
Are you doing okay?

00:11:50.532 --> 00:11:51.857
- This is really hard.

00:11:51.857 --> 00:11:52.790
(Hannah laughs)

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.220
- [Hannah] So happened here.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:57.160
- [Matt] Yeah. It didn't
quite come out like we wanted.

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:58.420
- [Hannah] Are you going to blend it?

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.750
- I'm gonna try about anything.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.454
- [Hannah] (laughs) Are you okay?

00:12:01.454 --> 00:12:02.411
- I'm disappointed.

00:12:02.411 --> 00:12:05.490
- [Hannah] (laughs) I'm
sure it's gonna be good.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.050
What went wrong with
that hollandaise sauce

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:09.620
is he used a fork to mix the eggs

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.890
and didn't fully mix them or aerate them.

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:13.760
So there were chunks
of egg white in there.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:16.060
So he threw it in the blender

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:19.540
and blended it to try to get
it a little more whipped.

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.290
- Didn't go as smoothly as I wanted.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:24.600
It was kind of a debacle,
Hannah had to save me twice.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:25.740
Hey, you know what?

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:29.560
We tried a really tricky
dish and she's happy.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.650
So that's all I counts.

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:31.980
- [Hannah] This looks amazing.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.710
I like my poached eggs on the firm side.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:36.085
So let's see how they did.

00:12:36.085 --> 00:12:37.500
Ooh! (gasps)

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:41.000
The egg was poached so perfectly.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.480
It was delicious.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.926
Oh wow.

00:12:43.926 --> 00:12:45.400
Thank you guys.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:47.550
Best mother's day brunch ever.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.040
And because it was mother's day,

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.340
Matt and the boys agreed to do the dishes

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.240
and I got that day off.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.820
By the end of the week I was so grateful

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:57.300
for all of the beautiful food.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.660
I was really proud of them
for all of the effort they put

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:00.493
into it.

00:13:00.493 --> 00:13:04.210
And I was also really ready
to start cooking again.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:07.190
You may see me do the majority
of the cooking and that's

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:08.800
because that's, what's fun for me.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.300
That's what I love to do.

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:13.430
But it was really fun to see
Matt take on all the cooking

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:14.263
for a week.

00:13:14.263 --> 00:13:15.160
So that's all for now.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:15.993
I'm Hannah.

00:13:15.993 --> 00:13:17.990
And please let me know on Instagram, who

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:20.190
does the cooking in your house and please

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:24.040
let Matt know what a good job
he did on all of his recipes.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:25.430
Now, if you'll excuse us

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:29.100
I have some cooking to do and
he has some cleaning to do.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.040
Till next time.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.090
- Bye guys.

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:34.007
(cheerful ukulele)

